"""Owner-side magnetic workflow provider (family ``ndfeb_magnetic_workflow_v1``).

A scenario calibration, not fitted physics. Intrinsic coercivity is a saturating
function of a boundary-isolation score; remanence scales with relative density and
as-sintered coercivity and falls with oxidation and high-temperature anneal steps;
a one-parameter demagnetization curve turns Br, Hci and loop shape into (BH)max.
All magnetic values are apparent reported quantities (no demagnetizing correction).

Anchor values, hidden relations, lots and pre-seeded batches live only in the
owner world configuration, never in this source. Each world re-inverts its own
anchors, so hidden choices move only directions that no released record fixes.
Densification reuses ``thermal_dose``; Archimedes and microscopy responses reuse
the reviewed workflow instrument functions unchanged. This module is an owner-side
native provider dependency and never an investigator answer key.
"""
